# Data-handling policy for this study directory.
#
# The parent orgs/personal/.gitattributes annexes everything by default
# (`* annex.largefiles=anything`) but carves out `**/*.md annex.largefiles=nothing`
# so human-authored docs stay readable in plain git. That carve-out is UNSAFE for
# the reconstruction payload, because DS_CASE_PGS_CANONICAL ships as a `.md` file
# (04_DATA_PAYLOAD/06_CASE_PGS_AND_CONTROL_AGGREGATES/IQ_PGS_caseonly.md) and
# contains 91 rows of pseudonymous individual case PGS. Without the override below
# it would be committed to GitHub as plaintext.
#
# Package rule (01_SCOPE_AND_AUTHORIZATION/DATA_SECURITY_AND_AI_RULES.md):
#   "Never upload individual PGS rows, workbook rows, sample tables, or other
#    restricted data to an external AI tool, public paste service, public
#    repository, or external/public cloud service."
#
# Annexed content is encrypted (encryption=hybrid) before it reaches the b2 or
# ipfs special remotes, and never enters the git object graph as plaintext.

# Entire data payload is restricted regardless of extension. Overrides the
# parent `**/*.md` carve-out because deeper .gitattributes win.
reconstruction-package-a-v1.1/04_DATA_PAYLOAD/**    annex.largefiles=anything

# Unpublished manuscript set under peer review at Scientific Reports.
# The parent default already annexes .docx/.csv; stated explicitly so the rule
# survives any future extension change (e.g. a .md conversion of the manuscript).
submission/**                                       annex.largefiles=anything

# This policy file and the human-authored index stay in plain git. Neither
# contains restricted rows — only structure, schemas, and field definitions,
# which DATA_SECURITY_AND_AI_RULES.md explicitly permits.
.gitattributes                                      annex.largefiles=nothing
README.md                                           annex.largefiles=nothing

# Audit implementation stays readable. The verifier attestation claims the
# reconstruction used "independently implemented code"; a reviewer cannot check
# that claim against an annex symlink. The code carries no restricted rows.
audit/code/**                                       annex.largefiles=nothing

# Top-level return tables are the audit trail (claim values, input hash audit,
# deviation log, software environment, visual QA, AI assistance log). They hold
# hashes, counts, aggregate statistics and prose only. The single-level glob
# deliberately does NOT reach the subdirectories below.
audit/return/KAWASAKI_PHASE5C_INDEPENDENT_RETURN/*.tsv   annex.largefiles=nothing
audit/return/KAWASAKI_PHASE5C_INDEPENDENT_RETURN/*.txt   annex.largefiles=nothing

# Bulk outputs stay annexed. M05 requires individual scores to remain inside the
# encrypted return package, and these two directories are where per-artifact
# outputs land — including, later, the Figure 4 chain. Annexing them by rule
# means a future individual-level file cannot reach plain git by accident.
audit/return/KAWASAKI_PHASE5C_INDEPENDENT_RETURN/02_ARTIFACT_FILES/**   annex.largefiles=anything
audit/return/KAWASAKI_PHASE5C_INDEPENDENT_RETURN/03_SOURCE_TABLES/**   annex.largefiles=anything

# Second code-independent reconstruction (2026-08-13). Same reasoning as the
# audit/return/ top-level carve-out above: the verification report, claim
# values, input hash audit, deviation log and AI assistance log are the audit
# trail, and hold hashes, counts, aggregate statistics and prose only. The
# report in particular must stay in plain git for the same reason audit/code/**
# does -- a reader cannot check a verification claim against an annex symlink.
# The staged files were scanned against all 91 pseudonymous case identifiers
# before commit, with zero hits.
#
# These are single-level globs. Anything added in a SUBDIRECTORY of this path
# stays annexed by the inherited default, so a future individual-level file
# cannot reach plain git by accident.
audit/run-2026-08-13/*.tsv                          annex.largefiles=nothing
audit/run-2026-08-13/*.pdf                          annex.largefiles=nothing
audit/run-2026-08-13/README.md                      annex.largefiles=nothing

# Result-lock submission: the archive hash, completion block and attestation.
# These carry no restricted rows and no passphrase; the archive itself and its
# plaintext tree are deliberately NOT in this repository.
audit/run-2026-08-13/lock-submission/*.txt          annex.largefiles=nothing
audit/run-2026-08-13/lock-submission/*.md           annex.largefiles=nothing

# Reconstruction source for the second run, same reasoning as audit/code/**:
# the attestation claims the reconstruction used independently implemented
# code, and a reader cannot check that claim against an annex symlink. Python
# source only, no restricted rows.
audit/run-2026-08-13/code/**                        annex.largefiles=nothing
